---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CTAButton from "../../components/CTAButton.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "What to Know Before Buying a Working-Line Puppy",
  mainEntityOfPage: "https://alliancek9dogs.com/resources/what-to-know-before-buying-a-working-line-puppy/",
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Alliance K9", url: "https://alliancek9dogs.com/" },
  publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Alliance K9", url: "https://alliancek9dogs.com/" },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What to Know Before Buying a Working-Line Puppy"
  description="Before buying a working-line Belgian Malinois or Dutch Shepherd puppy, understand drive, structure, training needs, home fit, and responsible placement."
  type="article"
  schema={articleSchema}
>
  <Section
    eyebrow="Working-Line Guide"
    title="What to Know Before Buying a Working-Line Puppy"
    headingLevel="h1"
    description="A working-line puppy can become a remarkable partner, but only when the buyer understands what the genetics are built to do."
  >
    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-8 max-w-3xl text-stone">
      <p>Working-line puppies are bred for engagement, athleticism, problem-solving, reward motivation, and the ability to do real work. Those traits can be valuable for SAR, active homes, protection development, obedience, and serious training, but they require daily direction.</p>
      <h2>Questions to Ask Yourself</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Do I have time for training every day?</li>
        <li>Am I prepared for a high-drive puppy with real outlets?</li>
        <li>Will I work with a trainer when needed?</li>
        <li>Does my household fit this puppy's temperament?</li>
        <li>Am I choosing based on fit rather than color or photos?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Responsible placement means matching puppy temperament to buyer goals. Alliance K9 screens homes because the right home gives the dog the best chance to succeed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <CTAButton href="/puppies/">View Available Puppies</CTAButton>
      <CTAButton href="/apply/" variant="secondary">Start Puppy Application</CTAButton>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
